  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 1202 AM MDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nSunday...will be identical to Saturday although it may be a degree \nhotter over the plains. Additionally, there will be a slightly \nbetter chance of convective showers over the mtns and they may \nproduce some locally wetting rains, especially over the CONTDVD \nregion. Also, the lee trough may be more pronounced on Sunday over \nthe plains and we may see a few more thunderstorms over the plains \nand DRY LIGHTNING may be more of a concern. Elevated fire weather \nconcerns will also be possible over the far eastern plains on Sunday.\n\nMonday and Tuesday, Continued hot on the plains, but we will see a \nbetter chance of showers and storm over the high country. There will \nbe more clouds so it will be somewhat cooler over the higher \nterrain. POPs on the plains will also increase a bit and we should \nsee more clouds plains. \n\nFrom Wednesday onwards, the monsoon moves in with authority! NBM \nviewer for many points across our region show high pops and \naccumulated rainfall is 1 to 2+ inches from mid week into next \nweekend. Temperatures are also much cooler, even reaching below \nnormal by later in the week. Although the cooler temperatures and \nrain will be much welcomed, flash flooding issues for the burn scars \nand urban areas mill likely become a concern.\n\nFolks who live in the Aspen Acres burn scar area are strongly \nencouraged to maintain a vigilant watch of weather forecasts \nstarting early this upcoming week, as we could once again see \nmultiple days of monsoonal heavy rains on the burn scar starting\naround mid week this upcoming week and lasting into next \nweekend. \\/Hodanish",
